Be5 24. d5 Bxb2 25. Rxb2 exd5 26. cxd5 Kf8 { We have reached an interesting rook endgame, which is somewhat typical of this pawn structure (once Black has released his position with ...c6-c5); therefore I will analyze a few variations to help explain Black's path to victory. } 27. Rbd2 Re8 28. Kg2 Ke7 29. Re3+ $6 ( { The best practical chance is probably } 29. d6 Kd8 30. Rd5 Re6 { and the d6-pawn becomes vulnerable as Black intends to follow up with ...Kc8-b7-c6 capturing it. } 31. a3 { Attempting to play b3-b4 to open the c-file and make the king manoeuvre difficult, is met by: } a5 $1 { ⩱ Winning this endgame with Black will not be simple, but at least White cannot easily secure a draw either. } ) 
